            <ArticleTitle>Opioid administration for severe neuropathic pain in a patient with depression and prior heroin use.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>176-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1212/01.CON.0000411563.41709.e3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The treatment of pain can raise ethical dilemmas. This article presents a case of a young woman with a pain crisis from severe neuropathic pain that is complicated by comorbidities of depression and prior (but not active) heroin use. Medical and ethical justifications for either withholding or providing opioids for her pain are examined. State and federal laws governing opioid prescriptions by physicians for pain management are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
